    "title": "Pentucket Regional Eighth Graders Collecting Clothing as Project 351 Ambassadors - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WHAV News Staff ,\n1 hours ago Three Pentucket eighth graders are leading a districtwide clothing drive to support children in need as part of their work as ambassadors for Project 351. Eighth-grade students Marina Bistany, Owen Potter and Louis Sayani are serving as the district’s Project 351 ambassadors this year. As part of the statewide service program, the students organized the clothing drive to benefit Cradles to Crayons, a nonprofit that provides clothing and other essentials to children facing clothing insecurity. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
